<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Solomon II of Imereti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1772">1772</a>–<a href="/years/1815">1815</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> II of Imereti was the last king of Imereti in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>, reigning from 1789 to 1810. He accepted a Russian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> in 1804 but resisted direct rule. In 1810 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> deposed him and annexed Imereti; he escaped to Ottoman territory and died in exile at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trabzon">Trabzon</a> in 1815.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/solomon-ii-of-imereti.jpg" alt="Solomon II of Imereti" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: archives.gov.ge · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Solomon_II.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
